label Day1_Departure1:
    "As she thinks about heading over to get some tacos, the thought of the day going by without her covering everything she wanted to cover fills her mind as she focuses on walking towards a quiet alley along a portion of a relatively new part of the church. Her stomach growling a bit as she toughs out a bit of hunger early in the morning, the snacks on her backpack rustling as she pauses for a moment and relaxes herself in the quiet church alleyway. She stands upright as if riding a surfboard and a moment of silence fills the air as she closes her eyes."

    "She jumps for a moment and hovers in the air as the inevitable return to Earth never falls and the roar of something deafening begins and her entire body is moved in unison with the object she landed onto. She opens her eyes and within seconds, she notices that she is reaching the distant clouds in the sky that she didn’t notice earlier as she leans further down and stares towards the earth beyond the cruise missile she now has manifested and riding like a surfboard. She quickly pushes the missile’s trajectory downward as it levels out and its roar fades to a hum to her ears, her body having adjusted to the ability she is blessed or cursed with."

    "As Yuliana steadies out on the missile, she looks around herself and the earth around her, it’s clear skies all around as the frigid air washes over her. Giving her a shiver but she has acclimated to the conditions from years of practice, despite the act of using her abilities being a punishable offense. It’s crazy to think about how much happened back from 2035 to the modern day in 2156."

    "In 2035, a wave unknown events occurred in the world where a massive wave of energy emanated from the center of the earth and caused people across the world to gain superpowers called Essence. The event, later called The Burst Event resulted in global instability and unrest. Nations like Russia collapsed under civil war while Europe reformed into a new superpower. For two decades, a state of lawlessness swept the globe until the rise of hero-civil servants developed and expanded from Europe due to legislative progress. "

    "The once United States boiled over into civil war in 2074 when the populus couldn’t come into agreement on how to address the subject of Freedom of Essence use, politics devolving into violence in the media and warring factions formed. The government attempted to use military force to quell rebel cells but it backfired spectacularly when the nation’s government collapsed in 2075 from an uprising, forcing their armed forces to flee to western allies. After 8 years of conflict, the United Nations intervened in the entire continent and effectively put an end to the war in 2084."

    "An indefinite occupation of the states and the establishment of a new European-like government called the Union of America was formed and crushed any and all rebel resistance, forcing them to flee to then failed narco-state of Mexico. By the 90s, so-called hero academies began to form in the nation from Europe, a beacon of hope for aspiring young men and women to become heroes for their community. Former US infrastructure was also restructured to be Europe-like after the former nation’s infrastructure crumbled due to war-lord violence and vast quantities of healthcare were deemed necessary in spite of fierce resistance from vocal minorities who cried for individual responsibility. By the turn of the century, the nation is rebuilt and fundamentally changed, echoes of a broken, violent past littering the land as quiet reminders of a system that failed to unknown events."

    "By the modern day of 2157, militaries are now nearly non-existent due to continually escalating Essence abilities, the last things clinging on a thread being air-forces as budget cuts to fund law enforcement increase. Even an experimental UA hero-core is fading as more effective private agencies regulated by government takes the reigns, only reserved now for elite individuals for government. A fact one is far too familiar with as she looks around to the world around her, seeing trains move around, buses ferry people abound, and cafes opening up, she can’t help but wonder sometimes…"

    "High in the sky, the young girl begins to descend as she realizes that she just zipped around in circles for a little while in deep thought of the past. Probably as free as one can get with their Essence in the world, unimpeded and unattainable to those interested in stopping her. But she has a day to seize, and friends to meet, being accepted into one of the top universities for heroic justice is exciting to her. Even more so when it’s the same university her father graduated from before entering the core. The contents engrained in her mind like it was yesterday…"

