label Day1_Park_1:
    "As the thought passes by her mind, she begins to return to reality as she approaches her destination, a quiet part of town with a park spacious enough for her to touchdown at as she begins to dive down onto the green grass below her before shooting her missile up. As she shoots it up, she grips it with her left arm as she plants her left foot on one of the makeshift foot-holders on the missile as its engine slows down. Her and the missile gradually descending before touching down on the green grass below, her right foot tapping the floor before her other foot followed. She looked to her left and sees a glimpse of the missile she rode on dematerializing away in white sparkles, a thing she never quite understood how it worked scientifically but just happens."

    "She sighs for a moment, glad to have landed once again safely and fairly gracefully."

    Yul "“Whew… well that’s one journey down, now… to the next”, she’d talk to herself as she looks around and thinks about what to do next. The park looks nice and empty, peaceful even on the warm morning as she hardly sees anyone outside of one woman with a large gut who she must have enjoyed all night or morning long, the thought filling her mind before shaking it off. She notices a nice patch of roses in the distance as the thought of stopping to smell the roses comes to mind."

