label Day1_Cafe1:

    "As she weighs her options, she opts to stick to plans that she agreed upon with her friends and walk over to a café that the three of them agreed on, birds chirping in the air as she walks towards a pretty generous walkway with a bounce in her step. Within moments, she is walking down the street and heading towards a pretty quiet café called “Mariella’s Café” as her gut aches a little. Hunger on her mind, she walks to entrance-side waiter as she reserves a table of three and heads over and takes a seat. The menu being the first thing on her mind after arriving to the small third space in the middle of a quiet community."

    Yul "(Well, I’m here… might as well wait for them and have breakfast, hmm. I wouldn’t mind going for a bit of strawberry waffles and hot chocolate again hehe~)"

    "She groans for a moment as she leans herself back and stretches on the chair as she feels a few parts of her back pop and a wave of relaxation fills her mind again. Despite being tired, she’s enjoying the moment as she waits for the waiter to come back. She takes a moment to admire the scenery around her as the soft chirping of birds fill the air, breaking the silence that is sparsely filled with those walking by on a casual Sunday morning. The café is nice and modest, full of simple Hispanic livery mixed in with antique 2020s decorations of various plant themed goodies. The dark-oak floors and oak seat furnishings meshing well with the latte-colored walls and floral art pieces livening up the little restaurant as she notices who seems to be a waiter heading her way… it looks like it’s snowing around his head."

    "“May I take your order miss?”, the white-haired waiter says as he puts up a little booklet and tablet with a card reader. The snow chilling the environment around him as his gray beanie and brown jacket gives a sense of warmth in spite of his chilling aura. To a certain extent, he looks cute that she could just eat him right up."

    Yul "“Uhh… I think I’ll have a Lat- I mean hot chocolate with strawberry waffles. Uh… do you mind if I do something to you real quick?”, Yuliana would say almost timidly before asking the waiter a seemingly normal question, in spite of the fact that what she’s about to do is far from it."

    "“Uh, sure? As long as it doesn’t take me out of a job”, the waiter awkwardly approved as her lowered her booklet to his side and plants both hands on his hips as if waiting unamused in the request."

    Yul "“Ok so I’m gonna see if I can guess your Essence, you should only feel… chilly-er? For just a moment, m’kay?~”, Yuliana playfully stated before closing her eyes and concentrating for a moment." 

    "“Uh oka-“"

    Yul "Before he even has a chance to fully respond, Yuliana opens her eyes and uses her second essence ability, as a wave of chills fills through the waiter’s body as if she is peering into his soul. Consequently, anyone behind him feels something similar, weakening with distance as Yuli sees who’s behind him through walls, just a mere 5 people of varying distances with her prime focus in front of her. A man with an essence of the icy environmental type, of the offensive variety."

    Yul "“Mmmmmm… does it happen to be an Snow-manifesting ability that turns anything within your grasp into a snowy-“, Yuliana states before she is interrupted by the waiter immediately."

    "“Ok what the Hell. What did you do?”, the guy in front of him said with a bit of a scowl, clearly unamused from the scare that the woman gave her."

    Yul "“It’s just a scanning essence, you’re fine. Sorry if it was uncomfortable, everyone said that it’s creepy when I do it”, she defensively stated as she held her hands up in front of her as if preparing for a blow."

    "“No shit… urrrghhh…”, the young man pauses before clasping his left hand on his face, he groans before recomposing himself, “Just… don’t do that again please, been a crazy enough week already.”"
    
    Yul "“Please don’t report me”, Yuliana worriedly says before clasping the back of her neck, awkwardly looking at him."

    "“I won’t… as long as you’re not just gonna dash. *sigh* That’ll be 35 euros”, the waiter said as he tapped away onto the little tablet on his arms before looking at Yuli with a bit of a concerned expression, “Cash or card?”"

    Yul "“Card, though how close was I?” Yuli stated as she held her card out to him as he grasped it."

    "“Well… you got some points right but mostly off. I can manipulate the environment around me to be freezing cold, freeze both bodies of water and items. That kinda stuff. Kinda useless in Canada but a bit more useful here. And you?”, The man seemingly says a bit more calmly as he hands back her card and puts his tablet to the side, he looks around briefly to see if anyone else is in need of serving before resuming after seeing nobody else yet."

    Yul "“Uhh… my essence involves both missiles and a sort of wallhack kinda thing… wait do you play videogames?”"

    "“No, wait missiles?”, the young man flatly stated before snapping to missile."

    Yul "“Ok, yea so I can basically make missiles from thin air and see people through walls and sorta guess out their quirks but it’s not that great yet? Does that make sense?”, she explained as clearly as possible, in a manner that would look anyone crazy if it weren’t for the fact that she looked incredibly approachable currently. “Though I can’t make things go boom… yet.”"

    "“I see. I assume you’re going to a hero college?”"

    Yul "“Well… almost, I start this Thursday. And you?”"

    "“What a coincidence, I also start this Thursday. What college?”"

    Yul "“Cam Poly, and you”"

    "“Same, new student?”"

    Yul "“Yep”"

    "“Damn, same here”"

    Yul "“Coool! So we’re both gonna be in the same cohort. Isn’t that exciting!?”"

    "“Eh… ok maybe a little.”, the young man calmly responded as if he’s not too excited about the prospects being in the same cohort."

    Yul "“Not excited? Eh that’s fair.”, the young woman responded back as she matched the tone of the conversation as it seemingly died down."

    "A silence is filled between the two for a brief moment as the silence of distant bird chirps and the occasional distant municipal bus is heard in the distance. The two briefly staring at each other as a cool wind passes by the corner of the café before the waiter raises his left arm behind his neck and chuckles slightly as the sound and sight of someone entering the café comes to view to the young woman." 

    "“Well, I’ll get your order started miss.”, the young man affirmed as he broke the silence and resumed work as he quietly walks away to the kitchen and returning to help seat the new customer."

    "A young but soft-looking woman enters the café in a green shirt and loose dark red pants that look comfortable, she is escorted to her table as her shoes clack on the tile floor for mere moments before being seated next the windows a few tables across from Yuliana. Her short brown hair complementing her humble attire as she smiles at the waiter as she is handed the café’s menu. It looks like she arrived prepared as she appears to have made an order as she hands over a card to the server before having her menu picked up. She looks nice and friendly as she pulls out her phone and appears to read something on her own."

    Yul "Yuliana can’t help but look at her for a moment as the act of waiting for her meal is killing her boredom before realizing that cell phones exist. She puts down her backpack and shuffles around inside as she looks for her phone, a Hauwi 89 Pro Slim Max, and finds it as she pulls it out and taps the sides."

    "It’s dead."

    Yul "“Great… I forgot to charge it again”, she mutters to herself as she rustles through her backpack and pulls out her phone’s power cable and plug. Within a second, she plugged it to the nearby outlet beside her and saw its screen indicate that it was charging."

    "Left with nothing else better to do, she stares and looks out the window seeing if anything is happening only to be reminded with twelve people walking by that it’s early in the morning and anyone not working is still asleep out here. She quietly shifts her attention to in front of her as she spaces out and hears no sign of her friends arriving anytime soon."

    "(Where are they? Didn’t we agree upon meeting here at 8:30 in the morning? Did something happen to them? No, can’t be, they’re the bestest, toughest nuts to jump I know of. Nobody can lick them or mug them… maybe it’s just traffic and the frigid weather slowing them down.)"
    "(mmmph… well whatever is happening, I just have to wait a bit longer before checking up on them.)"

    "Suddenly, movement in front of her snaps her out of her trance as she notices the customer in front of her receiving a drink. It looks like a small, steaming mug of… something along with a small croissant pastry. Coffee, Hot Chocolate, Tea? She can’t really tell but she looks friendly enough and she has nothing else to do, maybe she could say hi and pass the time as she waits for her phone to charge."

